Maintainer: Xiao Jing Guo <xiaojing.guo@nrcan-rncan.gc.ca>
Description: Offers tools for data formatting, identification of measurement
 anomalies, and classification of data quality using spatial comparisons and
 cross-correlation techniques. Integrates flexible 'detrending' and climate–growth
 modeling through Generalized Additive Mixed Models ('GAMMs'), enabling robust
 analyses of non-linear trends and 'autocorrelated' data. Supports standardized
 visual reporting, including data summaries, quality diagnostics,
 and model performance. Compatible with '.rwl' files and tailored for the Canadian
 Forest Service Tree-Ring Data ('CFS-TRenD') repository, providing a comprehensive
 and adaptable framework for 'dendrochronologists' working with large and complex
 datasets.
